<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῠώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>running, flowing</i>; of persons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. τὰ οὖρα</span>
			<i>incontinent</i> of urine, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				48
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέρμα πολὺ καὶ ῥ</span>.
				<i>flowing freely</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				86c
			</span></i>, cf. d; of fevers, <i>continuous</i> or <i>frequent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.552
			</span></i> (nisi <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοώδης</span>
		legend.).</div>
